    <strong>What to notice:</strong> each question rehearses one reading of the map —
    lever-rule arithmetic, the eutectic's casting behaviour, cementite's role in steel, and
    the battery plateau as a two-phase field. The wrong options are the tempting misreadings:
    the "strongest" composition, special eutectic atoms, voltage as a fuel gauge. If the
    fourth question surprises you, reread the battery section — the phase diagram is doing
    the same work there, just read sideways.
  </p>
